@startuml
' NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram: UC3 Process Rental, start the rental and identify the customer (Contracts 10 to 12), W11 draft
' Team D - editable source of assets/dsd_uc3_start_rental.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng assets/dsd_uc3_start_rental.puml
' Participants: classes of the logical view (architecture.md 4.2) and of the design class diagram skeleton. Operations: system_interfaces.md 3.4 and 4.3.
' Messages marked <<new>> are not in the logical view or in system_interfaces.md yet (sent to Borja for the design class diagram).

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #444444
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam BoxPadding 6
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F4F8FD
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam SequenceDividerBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B8A04A
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam LegendBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 190

title NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram: UC3 Process Rental, start and customer (Contracts 10-12)

box "UI layer (ui.api)" #F4F8FD
  participant ":Rental\nController" as Ctl
end box
box "Application / domain layer" #F4F8FD
  participant ":Rental\nHandler" as H
  participant "session:\nCashierSession" as S
  participant "rental:\nRental" as R
  participant "open:\nRental" as O
  participant "customer:\nCustomer" as C
end box
box "application.interfaces (storage, AD-05)" #F4F8FD
  participant ":Transaction\nRepository" as Repo
  participant ":StoreDatabase\nSync" as Sync
end box

== makeNewRental() - Contract 10 ==
[-> Ctl : POST /api/rentals
Ctl -> H : makeNewRental()
H -> Repo : nextTransactionID()
Repo --> H : id (e.g. R03-000161)
H -> S : createRental(id) <<new>>
S -> R ** : create(id, session)
note right of R
  isComplete = false, rentalDate = today.
  The session records its transactions (Creator).
  Nothing is saved yet: a rental exists in the
  database only from the payment (state diagram 7.2).
end note
S --> H : rental
H --> Ctl : rental ID
[<-- Ctl : 201 rental ID

== enterCustomerID(customerID) - Contract 11 ==
[-> Ctl : PUT /api/rentals/{rentalID}/customer {"customerID"}
Ctl -> H : enterCustomerID(customerID)
H -> Repo : findCustomer(customerID) <<new>>
note right of Repo
  Local copy of the table customer, copied down
  from the store database every 5 min (AD-05).
end note
Repo --> H : Optional<Customer>
alt customer not found (4a)
  H --> Ctl : unknown customer
  [<-- Ctl : 404 "Customer ID not found":\nenter it again or register a new customer
else customer found
  H -> Repo : findOpenRentalsOfCustomer(customerID) <<new>>
  Repo --> H : open rentals on this register
  opt store database reachable
    H -> Sync : findOpenRentalsOfCustomer(customerID) <<new>>
    Sync --> H : open rentals at the other registers
  end
  loop each open rental
    H -> O : hasOverdueLine(today) <<new>>
    note right of O
      Information Expert: each RentalLineItem
      knows /isOverdue from its due date (DR-06).
    end note
    O --> H : true or false
  end
  alt an open rental is overdue (5a)
    H --> Ctl : overdue rental
    [<-- Ctl : 409 "This customer has an overdue rental\nand cannot start a new one" (BR-12)
  else no overdue rental
    H -> R : setCustomer(customer) <<new>>
    H --> Ctl : customer accepted
    [<-- Ctl : 200 customer accepted
  end
end
note over H, Sync
  Store database NOT_AVAILABLE: only the rentals of this register are checked. The store accepts
  this risk and relies on the deposit, as for a customer who registers again (BR-12, SRS 5.3 Q5).
end note

== registerCustomer() - Contract 12 (ext. 4a.3) ==
[-> Ctl : POST /api/rentals/{rentalID}/customer
Ctl -> H : registerCustomer()
H -> Repo : nextCustomerID() <<new>>
note right of Repo
  register ID + customer_counter of
  register_state, e.g. R03-000012 (data model, DC-09)
end note
Repo --> H : customerID
H -> R : registerNewCustomer(customerID) <<new>>
R -> C ** : create(customerID)
note right of C
  The customer ID only, no other personal data
  (DR-18, NFR-12). A new customer has no rental
  history, so no overdue check (UC3 4a.3).
  The customer is saved with the rental
  (saveCompleted): a cancelled rental saves none.
end note
R --> H : customer
H --> Ctl : new customer ID
[<-- Ctl : 201 new customer ID, linked to the rental

legend bottom left
  **GRASP**
  Controller: RentalController receives the system operations of S-08 and gives them to RentalHandler (one handler per use case).
  Creator: CashierSession creates the Rental, because the session records its transactions (Contract 10); Rental creates the new Customer,
  because the rental is the first to use it and the customer is saved with it (Contract 12).
  Information Expert: each open Rental answers whether it has an overdue line, from the due dates of its RentalLineItems (BR-12).
  Indirection, Protected Variations: the handler sees only TransactionRepository and StoreDatabaseSync; the local and the store
  database (AD-05) can change without changing the handler.
  Pure Fabrication: TransactionRepository makes the IDs and keeps the customers; it is not a concept of the store.
endlegend
@enduml
